    "sourceGaps": [
      "1991E1: The obtained collection contains neither the separate answer sheet nor a participant's titration volumes or pH measurements. Its key explicitly expects measured entries for 1.3 and 1.4; numeric experimental answers and a numeric acid $\\mathrm pK_a$ cannot be fabricated. All five connected requests remain in this one practical problem.\n\nAttributed archive/compiler source: Anton Sirota (editor), *The Competition Problems from the International Chemistry Olympiads*, Volume 2, IChO International Information Centre, Bratislava, IUVENTA, 2009. Retain the teaching-copy/distribution attribution and rights notice; no broader commercial licence or unchanged complete jury edition is asserted.",
      "1991E2: The bottle concentrations, ionic activity-coefficient values, separate answer sheet, experimental temperature and measured $E_A,E_B,E_C$ are not supplied in these obtained pages. The native key gives procedures and symbolic formulas; numerical stability constants cannot be fabricated. The question uses $K_B,K_C$ while the key uses $\\beta_4$. The key's double equals sign in the $E'_1$ expression is retained. Several mathematical operator and Greek glyphs are absent in the native page raster although represented in its text layer; their text-layer identities are used in the editable equations, without silently replacing the printed double equals sign. All six connected requests and the four procedure sections remain one experiment.\n\nAttributed archive/compiler source: Anton Sirota (editor), *The Competition Problems from the International Chemistry Olympiads*, Volume 2, IChO International Information Centre, Bratislava, IUVENTA, 2009. Retain the teaching-copy/distribution attribution and rights notice; no broader commercial licence or unchanged complete jury edition is asserted."
